  "raw_meta_yaml": "{% set version = \"2026.2\" %}\n# v2026.2's DEPS pins headers at vulkan-sdk-1.4.350.1, but we intentionally build\n# against the newer vulkan-sdk-1.4.357.0 headers (the DEPS pin of the SPIRV-Tools\n# vulkan-sdk-1.4.357.0 tag, which contains v2026.2): the run_constrained below pins\n# downstream consumers to the headers we build with, and intel-graphics-compiler\n# >=2.40 needs SPV_INTEL_predicated_io from headers 1.4.357.0.\n{% set headers_version = \"1.4.357.0\" %}\n\npackage:\n  name: spirv-tools\n  version: \"{{ version }}\"\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Tools/archive/refs/tags/v{{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: b4390652e64ab188eede9d556cf183b3c1c4be44d4fcd104b0d4af3bea2712d1\n  patches:\n    - 0001-Get-package-version-and-description-from-conda-build.patch\n    # SPIRV-Headers 1.4.357.0's grammar adds the GatherModes operand kind\n    # (SPV_QCOM_image_processing3); backport the upstream support so the\n    # generated tables compile:\n    # https://github.com/KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Tools/commit/7fa1f024cf86890b2f9ac2aab19d0583cea59277\n    - 0002-backport-SPV_QCOM_image_processing3-operand-support.patch\n    # 1.4.357.0 also adds five FPEncoding enumerants (SPV_EXT_ocp_microscaling_types)\n    # not covered by an exhaustive switch, tripping -Werror=switch; map them to\n    # SPV_FP_ENCODING_UNKNOWN.  Superseded by upstream f80351511e in v2026.3.\n    - 0003-handle-ocp-microscaling-fp-encodings.patch\n\nbuild:\n  run_exports:\n    # They seem to be using calver, so their version numbers are not very informative\n    # But we expect these to be rather stable\n    # so lets try 'x' https://github.com/conda-forge/spirv-tools-feedstock/issues/3\n    - {{ pin_subpackage('spirv-tools', 'x') }}\n  number: 3\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - {{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - {{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - cmake\n    - make    # [unix]\n    - ninja   # [win]\n    - python\n  host:\n    - spirv-headers {{ headers_version }}\n  run_constrained:\n    - {{ pin_compatible('spirv-headers', max_pin='x.x.x.x') }}\n\ntest:\n  requires:\n    - {{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - {{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - cmake\n    - ninja\n  files:\n    - test/CMakeLists.txt\n    - test/main.cpp\n  commands:\n    - spirv-as -h\n    - cmake -G Ninja -S test -B test-build\n    - cmake --build test-build\n    - ./test-build/test-spirv-tools  # [unix]\n    - test-build\\\\test-spirv-tools.exe  # [win]\n\nabout:\n  home: https://github.com/KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Tools\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: The SPIR-V Tools project provides an API and commands for processing SPIR-V modules.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - oleksandr-pavlyk\n    - ZzEeKkAa\n    - isuruf\n    - hmaarrfk\n    - JarrettSJohnson\n    # baszalmstra is insterested in helping windows failures\n    - baszalmstra\n",
